			<item>
				<title>qmk keyboard</title>
				<link>https://muwat0.github.io/posts/qmk/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 09 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>murat@muwat.org (murat)</author>
				<guid>https://muwat0.github.io/posts/qmk/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I didn&amp;rsquo;t know my keyboard (Glorious GMMK 2 96% ISO) supports QMK firmware. I didn&amp;rsquo;t even hear about QMK while buying this keyboard back then. A couple days ago, while mindlessly scrolling YT videos, I saw a video about home row mods. I&amp;rsquo;ve heard about that in the past and always thought this thing is doable by only using custom open motherboards and self-built microcontroller keyboards. I&amp;rsquo;m too dumb so I didn&amp;rsquo;t realize my keyboard is a prebuilt custom keyboard. So turns out my keyboard supports QMK.&#xA;I began exploring QMK. I had a couple issues with QMK Linux dependencies (Arch Linux Python pip env related problems) and fixed them by just installing packages with sudo.&#xA;&lt;img src=&#34;https://muwat0.github.io/images/fkitmacrowave.gif&#34; alt=&#34;fuck it&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
